{title: Wayfaring Stranger}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
I'm just a [Am]poor wayfaring [Dm]stranger,
[Am]traveling through this [E]world of [Am]woe.
But there's no [Am]sickness, toil, nor [Dm]danger,
in that [Am]bright land to [E]which I [Am]go.

{c: Verse 2}
I'm [Am]going there to see my [Dm]Father,
[Am]I'm going there no [E]more to [Am]roam.
I'm only [Am]going over [Dm]Jordan,
I'm only [Am]going [E]over [Am]home.
